From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 2 Oct 2026 11:17:34 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 116/116] No stem export while the output is being resampled:
 no E242, no second recorder

SHIFT + RECORD records the output through the audio recorder (resampling).
SAVE + RECORD (and the song menu's export) then started a stem export: the
views check playback and song recording, not the audio recorder, and the
export set up its own output recording. A beta build froze with E242 in
AudioRecorder::setupRecordingToFile() (the fuzzer's seed 226, second boot,
stop run 9); a release build replaced the running recorder.
StemExport::startStemExportProcess() now refuses while the audio recorder
records, with the views' "can't export stems" popup.

Test (beta-1.3/tests/repro/stem_export_resampling_emu.py): SHIFT + RECORD,
SAVE + RECORD: the popup, the resampling goes on (before: E242); a short
RECORD press then ends it.
---
 src/deluge/processing/stem_export/stem_export.cpp | 7 +++++++
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/deluge/processing/stem_export/stem_export.cpp b/src/deluge/processing/stem_export/stem_export.cpp
index 1cbffa98..bfa00503 100644
--- a/src/deluge/processing/stem_export/stem_export.cpp
+++ b/src/deluge/processing/stem_export/stem_export.cpp
@@ -83,6 +83,13 @@ StemExport::StemExport() {
 /// starts stem export process which includes setting up UI mode, timer, and preparing
 /// instruments / clips / kit rows for exporting
 void StemExport::startStemExportProcess(StemExportType stemExportType) {
+	// The export records the output through the audio recorder. While that already records (resampling, started with
+	// SHIFT + RECORD), a second recording would replace its recorder: E242 in a beta build, a lost recorder otherwise
+	if (audioRecorder.recordingSource > AudioInputChannel::NONE) {
+		display->displayPopup(deluge::l10n::get(deluge::l10n::String::STRING_FOR_CANT_EXPORT_STEMS));
+		return;
+	}
+
 	// in case playback is active when you start stem export, stop it.
 	stopPlayback();
 
